/**
 * What each muscle is and does, one line per muscle (Gray's Anatomy 42nd ed.; OpenStax A&P 2e ch. 11;
 * Kendall's Muscles; Moore's Clinically Oriented Anatomy). Fields, separated by " | ":
 *   name | origin | insertion | nerve | roots | actions | blood supply | slow-twitch % | note
 * Actions are movement ids from joints.ts with the direction of the LEFT-hand muscle: `elbow-flex+` takes the
 * slider towards its flexion end, `forearm-pron-` towards supination; `*` marks a prime mover (the rest assist).
 * For a muscle on the right the signs of the trunk, neck and jaw side and rotation movements are mirrored.
 * Slow-twitch % is the typical type I share (a teaching figure; people vary widely). `-` where nothing is added.
 */

